    "narrative": "The heart of today\u2019s lineup is anchored by **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (79.47) and **Daulton Varsho** (71.99), our premier plays for this slate. **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** benefits from a high-leverage spot against Framber Valdez; his ability to exploit the pitcher's slow delivery makes him a primary target for stolen base accumulation, a critical focus for LawDog given the league's scarcity. Meanwhile, **Daulton Varsho** earns his elite marks due to an excellent matchup against Houser, whose 4.73 xERA provides a clear runway for high-efficiency production. **Jonathan Aranda** and **Dylan Beavers** round out our top-tier targets, both surging past the 60-point threshold on the back of favorable platoon splits and park factors, with **Dylan Beavers** specifically identified for his potential to exploit the opposing pitcher's tempo to boost our SB total.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today involved **Gavin Sheets**, who narrowly missed the cut with a 47.64 score. While he presents a solid platoon advantage against May, he lacked the explosive upside required to displace the high-floor efficiency provided by **Brendan Donovan** or **Luis Arraez**. We are closely monitoring the lineup status for **Gleyber Torres**; should he be dropped from the #2 spot, his score\u2014currently propped up by a strong 13% platoon boost against Griffin\u2014could see a slight downward revision, though he remains a strong start in the interim. Outside of the lineup, **Justin Crawford** occupies a precarious position at the #9 spot against Leahy; while he carries a usable 51.91, his value is severely dampened by his low slot in the order, serving as a reminder that we are prioritizing volume of at-bats alongside raw talent to remain competitive in Roto scoring.",
